Type: Package
Package: LLMRpanel
Title: Calibrated Silicon Samples for Survey and Experiment Design
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ali", "Sanaei", , "sanaei@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantitative silicon sampling that requires a recorded calibration
  comparison before any human-population claim, built on 'LLMR'. Persona panels
  are drawn from user-supplied population margins. Survey and experimental
  instruments, such as Likert items and conjoint tasks, are administered with
  item- and option-order randomization. Every result object carries a calibration
  slot and prints an UNCALIBRATED banner until benchmark comparison fills it. The
  package's stance is printed into its objects: silicon panels are design-stage
  tools for pretesting instruments and analyzing power, and for measuring model
  behavior. They do not estimate human population quantities unless calibration
  earns that reading.
